[Music]  my name is tintin zhou and i'm a  neuroscientist at the mcgovern institute  at mit  imagine for a second that you're a mouse  and you really like to eat a piece of  cheese but in order to get the cheese  you must remember the color of this  light you can't forget it even after  light turns off right now your most  brain is holding this important  information in an area called the  prefrontal cortex and when you have to  remember which light you saw earlier  you'll probably guess correctly this is  called working memory the mice in my lab  have difficulty with working memory they  have schizophrenia a serious brain  disorder that affects the ability to  think clearly they can now remember  information for more than a few seconds  because they have mistakes in their dna  and their prefrontal cortex doesn't  connect properly to other parts of the  brain i'm studying how we can fix the  genes and the abnormal brain connections  associated with schizophrenia so that  all mice and people can live a rewarding  life

